# /uploads/ directory policy
#
# Files here are artwork submitted through the Upload Art form. The operator
# CAN still retrieve any file directly by its exact URL, e.g.
#   https://becreativetx.com/uploads/20260726-141530_ab12cd34_logo.pdf
# ...or over SFTP / hPanel File Manager. What is blocked below is directory
# BROWSING (so the list of everyone's files is not public) and any attempt to
# execute an uploaded file as a script.

# 1. No directory listing.
Options -Indexes

# 2. Never run uploaded files as code. Extensions are validated on upload, but
#    this is defense in depth in case something slips through.
<FilesMatch "\.(php|php3|php4|php5|php7|phtml|pht|cgi|pl|py|sh|asp|aspx)$">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# 3. Force downloads and stop content-type sniffing. This neutralizes stored
#    XSS from types like .svg being opened inline in the browser.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
    Header set Content-Disposition "attachment"
    Header set X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
</IfModule>
